  "summary": "Full assessment of all 276 French/Vietnamese passages of the title story, from the retreating army in Rouen through the coach, the inn at Tôtes and the Prussian officer’s demand to the closing Marseillaise sob. The first reviews scored 8.375 and 8.55 and found one major (the lost ‘Loiseau vole’ pun); it was fixed with about seventy other edits. Fresh separate-context reviews of the revised text scored 8.73 (units 1–140) and 8.675 (units 141–276) with no major or critical finding, and twenty-eight minor points were then applied. On the half-point scale the final score is 8.675, above the unchanged 8.6 threshold. No unresolved major or critical issue remains.",
  "title_review": {
    "source_title": "Boule de Suif",
    "target_title": "Cục Mỡ (Boule de Suif)",
    "rationale": "Boule de Suif keeps the French title of the story; the nickname is explained in the Vietnamese text as ‘Cục Mỡ’."
  }
